BT /Fb 22 Tf 1 0 0 1 72 700 Tm (Folding a dart) Tj ET
BT /Fi 12 Tf 1 0 0 1 72 676 Tm (Letter or A4. Work on a table. Sharp creases fly straighter.) Tj ET
BT /Fr 12 Tf 1 0 0 1 72 640 Tm (1.  Fold the sheet in half the long way. Open it again. The) Tj ET
BT /Fr 12 Tf 1 0 0 1 72 622 Tm (    centre crease is the spine.) Tj ET
BT /Fr 12 Tf 1 0 0 1 72 604 Tm (2.  Fold the top two corners down to the spine so they meet) Tj ET
BT /Fr 12 Tf 1 0 0 1 72 586 Tm (    in a point. This is the nose.) Tj ET
BT /Fr 12 Tf 1 0 0 1 72 568 Tm (3.  Fold the long edges in to the spine. The nose gets) Tj ET
BT /Fr 12 Tf 1 0 0 1 72 550 Tm (    sharper. Crease firmly with a thumbnail.) Tj ET
BT /Fr 12 Tf 1 0 0 1 72 532 Tm (4.  Fold the plane in half along the spine, printed side out.) Tj ET
BT /Fr 12 Tf 1 0 0 1 72 514 Tm (5.  Fold each wing down so the top edge of the wing lines) Tj ET
BT /Fr 12 Tf 1 0 0 1 72 496 Tm (    up with the bottom of the fuselage. Leave a finger of) Tj ET
BT /Fr 12 Tf 1 0 0 1 72 478 Tm (    body under the wings.) Tj ET
BT /Fr 12 Tf 1 0 0 1 72 460 Tm (6.  Pinch the fuselage. Hold it under the wings, a little) Tj ET
BT /Fr 12 Tf 1 0 0 1 72 442 Tm (    behind the nose. Throw level, not up. A gentle toss.) Tj ET
BT /Fh 9 Tf 1 0 0 1 72 72 Tm (Page 2 of 3  ∑  public domain  ∑  sample packed in the app) Tj ET
endstream
endobj
