0 0 0 rg
BT /Fb 22 Tf 1 0 0 1 72 700 Tm (Why it glides) Tj ET
BT /Fr 12 Tf 1 0 0 1 72 664 Tm (Four forces, same as any aeroplane, just quieter.) Tj ET
BT /Fr 12 Tf 1 0 0 1 72 646 Tm () Tj ET
BT /Fr 12 Tf 1 0 0 1 72 628 Tm (Lift comes from air moving faster over the top of the wing) Tj ET
BT /Fr 12 Tf 1 0 0 1 72 610 Tm (than under it. A paper dart is a poor aerofoil, but a good) Tj ET
BT /Fr 12 Tf 1 0 0 1 72 592 Tm (enough one if the wings are even and the nose is not too) Tj ET
BT /Fr 12 Tf 1 0 0 1 72 574 Tm (heavy.) Tj ET
BT /Fr 12 Tf 1 0 0 1 72 556 Tm () Tj ET
BT /Fr 12 Tf 1 0 0 1 72 538 Tm (Weight is the paper. A slightly heavier nose keeps the dart) Tj ET
BT /Fr 12 Tf 1 0 0 1 72 520 Tm (from stalling. A paper-clip on the tip is a trim tab.) Tj ET
BT /Fr 12 Tf 1 0 0 1 72 502 Tm () Tj ET
BT /Fr 12 Tf 1 0 0 1 72 484 Tm (Thrust is your throw. After that there is only glide. Drag is) Tj ET
BT /Fr 12 Tf 1 0 0 1 72 466 Tm (everything that is not smooth: a puffy crease, a bent wing,) Tj ET
BT /Fr 12 Tf 1 0 0 1 72 448 Tm (a throw that starts the plane tumbling.) Tj ET
BT /Fr 12 Tf 1 0 0 1 72 430 Tm () Tj ET
BT /Fr 12 Tf 1 0 0 1 72 412 Tm (If it dives, unfold a millimetre of up-elevator at the back of) Tj ET
BT /Fr 12 Tf 1 0 0 1 72 394 Tm (each wing. If it stalls, add a little weight to the nose. If it) Tj ET
BT /Fr 12 Tf 1 0 0 1 72 376 Tm (rolls, the wings are not the same. Make them the same.) Tj ET
